From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:37:13 +0000
Subject: Test ScreenSaver inhibitors as the session manager sees them

test-listener-inhibit runs in make check: the real listener on a private
session bus, a stand-in org.gnome.SessionManager and callers on their own
connections, one process per case: forwarding with the idle flag on both
object paths, release on UnInhibit (not on another sender's), before the
session manager answered and when the caller goes away, a caller changing
a well-known name keeps its inhibitor, no session manager, empty strings,
and nothing reaching a new session manager.

The listener needs its logind session at start. The harness puts it on
the logind path it takes on the target, without touching the files under
test: DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS and DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS point at two
private buses; a stand-in org.freedesktop.login1 answering only
GetSessionByPID is served from its own thread on the system bus;
XDG_SESSION_PATH is a dummy path, XDG_SESSION_ID is unset; the test is
linked with --wrap=access so that the listener sees /run/systemd/seats/.
The harness checks its own setup before each case.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
